Revision history for Perl module Locale::Unicode::RBNF

v0.1.1 2026-10-26T08:32:45+0900
    - On a perl with long double or __float128 numbers, non-integral parse results are
      now rounded to double, as the C engine and ICU return them. The pure-Perl engine
      previously computed them with the wider precision, so t/05.xs.t failed on such
      perls (CPAN Testers, reported by Slaven Rezić, issue #1).
    - Makefile.PL now stops with "OS unsupported" on a perl with 32-bit integers, which
      the int64 arithmetic does not support (CPAN Testers armv6l and i686 reports).

v0.1.0 2026-10-23T21:10:33+0900
    - Initial release: port from ICU4C 79.1 RuleBasedNumberFormat (rbnf.cpp, nfrs.cpp,
      nfrule.cpp, nfsubs.cpp), with a loader for the CLDR RBNF, number symbols, numbering
      systems and plural rules data.
